(PRC-10 — `Change directory to "<path>".` performs chdir(2), and later
 relative paths resolve from the new working directory.
 The probe changes into its scratch directory, creates a child there by a
 BARE relative name, changes back with "..", and then finds that child at
 the path it would only have if the chdir really took effect.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-10.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the working directory really moved
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_cd".
Change directory to "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_cd".
Create a directory called "made_from_inside".
Change directory to "../../..".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_cd/made_from_inside" is available then, print "the working directory really moved".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_cd/made_from_inside".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_cd".
